Abaqus version list (admin task)
================================

The version dropdown lists ../module_versions/<cluster>.json, one file per cluster.
Each option's value is the "module load" argument (e.g. "ABAQUS/2025"). The form only
reads the file; it never runs "module spider".

Build or refresh it on each cluster where the environment is offered, and again after
an ABAQUS version is installed or removed there:

  ./generate_module_versions.py ABAQUS

Without a file for a cluster the dropdown says "Not configured on this cluster".
generate_module_versions.py is the same script as in the R environment.

Compiler for user subroutines (optional)
----------------------------------------
A job with a user subroutine loads a compiler module. The default is intel-compilers/2023.2.1
(ifort 2021.10 and ifx). To use another one per Abaqus version, add
../module_versions/<cluster>.compilers.json, e.g.

  { "ABAQUS/2025": "intel-compilers/2023.2.1", "default": "intel-compilers/2023.2.1" }

It must match the compiler in the Abaqus site abaqus_v6.env (compile_fortran / link_sl).
